# Title: File Download From Browser Process Via Inline URL
# ID: 94771a71-ba41-4b6e-a757-b531372eaab6
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-01-11
# Tags: attack.command-and-control, attack.t1105
# Description: Detects execution of a browser process with a URL argument pointing to a file with a potentially interesting extension. This can be abused to download arbitrary files or to hide from the user for example by launching the browser in a minimized state.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((cmdline:*.7z OR cmdline:*.dat OR cmdline:*.dll OR cmdline:*.exe OR cmdline:*.hta OR cmdline:*.ps1 OR cmdline:*.psm1 OR cmdline:*.txt OR cmdline:*.vbe OR cmdline:*.vbs OR cmdline:*.zip)) OR ((cmdline:*.7z\"* OR cmdline:*.dat\"* OR cmdline:*.dll\"* OR cmdline:*.hta\"* OR cmdline:*.ps1\"* OR cmdline:*.psm1\"* OR cmdline:*.txt\"* OR cmdline:*.vbe\"* OR cmdline:*.vbs\"* OR cmdline:*.zip\"*))) AND (cmdline:*http*) AND ((process_name:*\\brave.exe OR process_name:*\\chrome.exe OR process_name:*\\msedge.exe OR process_name:*\\opera.exe OR process_name:*\\vivaldi.exe)))
